const PRIOR = {"V1": {"diffHash": "a4a0ce36c95e3c628d32713a6b360cb35dcede3e", "summary": "I rebuilt the Core v2 server flow and the Core client effects. Nothing has been run in Studio (builders may not use it). I checked every clause by reading and tracing the code paths. C2 passes from the worktree root: rojo build succeeds, selene reports 0 errors (its 7 warnings are all in the frozen UIKit/Core.lua), and stylua --check is clean. Only my own paths changed (C1).\n\nWhat each clause relies on:\n\n- **V1-1 Boot:** `Places.ensureLobby()` calls `Lobby.build(LOBBY_CENTER)` once at boot, inside a pcall; if it errors, a plain grass pad is used instead. It removes any `Lobby` model left in workspace from an edit-mode build. If the model has no PrimaryPart, its WorldPivot is set to LOBBY_CENTER, so the pivot check passes whatever layout the World piece uses. The lobby is only rebuilt if it disappears from workspace (checked by the rescue loop), so the instance stays the same across rounds. All per-round destroy/build calls and every Stands call are gone.\n- **V1-2 Join square:** `Join.lua` checks every 0.2 s whether the root is inside the `JOIN_ZONE_SIZE` box on top of PlayZone (rotation-safe, 1 stud tolerance below the pad top). It writes Player `Queued` and GameState `QueuedCount`. If PlayZone is missing (true with the old Lobby.lua in this worktree), it uses LOBBY_CENTER+(0,0,36) and warns once. `Debug_AutoQueue` queues everyone not playing.\n  - `runLobby`: when the timer ends with nobody queued it sets LobbyHold=true and PhaseEnd=0. The first step-in sets LobbyHold=false, PhaseStart=now and PhaseEnd=now+LOBBY_HOLD_RESTART. This restart countdown is never shortened by FastIntermission, so it matches the clause's 8 s timing.\n  - Every phase writes PhaseStart. Waiting is used only when nobody is in the main game. Participants are queued, not InSolo, alive, capped at 12, sorted with the v1 longest-waiting tiebreak; overflow players get a \"Round full\" toast.\n- **V1-3 Vote:** `Vote.lua` picks options in this order: games that fit the expected player count and were not just played, then games needing more players, then last round's game. The expected count is max(QueuedCount, players in the main game), because QueuedCount is almost always 0 when the lobby starts.\n  - `Core_Vote` checks that the id is one of the options, the player is Queued, and `VOTE_RATE_LIMIT` has passed; invalid ids are rejected without using up the rate limit. Leaving the square clears the vote, and VoteCounts is recounted as JSON `{id: n}` on every change.\n  - Resolution: `Debug_ForceMinigame`, then `Debug_ForceVote`, else the most votes among options whose MinPlayers \u2264 participants (ties and no-votes random). If every option needs more players, a random eligible id from the whole pool is used.\n  - RouletteReel is 15\u201320 ids from the options (plus a forced or fallback id), ending on MinigameId. MinigameInfo now also publishes MinPlayers, Icon and Color.\n- **V1-4 Elimination:**\n  - Context: a fall below killY, Humanoid death, or `ctx.eliminate` now eliminates. The respawn path runs only when `fallRule == \"respawn\"`; `Debug_NoEliminate` respawns on the map.\n  - killY = max(map KillY, center.Y \u2212 KILL_DEPTH).\n  - Death.lua, at the moment of elimination:\n    - InRound=false and Eliminated=true (Eliminated is set first).\n    - \"splash\" for falls, sent when the body reaches the water, then the body is anchored there for the beat. \"poof\" for other reasons, \"boom\" for bomb reasons, plus \"ko\" when someone gets the credit.\n    - `Announce.big(victim, \"OUT!\", \"#p of n\")` and the feed line.\n  - After DEATH_BEAT (1 s) the player goes to a lobby spawn and gets `Core_Death` with the ARCHITECTURE payload. Spectating is never set automatically, and the rescue loop skips players during the beat.\n- **V1-5 Death choice:** `Core_DeathChoice` accepts only \"spectate\" or \"lobby\", ignores players in Solo or alive in the round, and is rate limited to 0.3 s. Inside the cooldown the latest choice is kept and applied when the cooldown ends, so spectate then lobby fired quickly still ends with Spectating=false. Spectating also points the player's ReplicationFocus at the arena (only matters if streaming is on).\n- **V1-6 Revive:** `Revive.status`/`Revive.revive` with the Config rules. `Debug_FreeRevive` offers a revive even with 1 participant and keeps the round open until the window closes. \"used\" is checked before \"round over\", so a second elimination reports \"used\".\n  - `ctx:_revive`: alive again, placement removed, placed at `session:onRevive` or a random spawn, character ShieldUntil = now + SPAWN_SHIELD once placed. It then synchronously calls onRevived (InRound/Eliminated/Spectating, Alive, Signals.PlayerRevived, \"<Name> is back!\"); it refuses a second revive in the same round.\n  - The documented way to reach the live Context is `require(Core.State).mainContext()`. If the command bar or execute_luau runs in a separate Luau VM, Revive and mainContext forward through a BindableFunction \"CoreApi\", returning a proxy whose calls run on the live ctx.\n- **V1-7 KO credit:** `ctx.knockback(p, dir, power, stun, attacker)` returns false when the player is not alive or shielded. `ctx.credit` ignores self-credit and sets LastHitBy/LastHitAt; `ctx.isShielded` is added. An elimination within KO_CREDIT_WINDOW credits the killer: Player KOs +1 (reset at Intro), the killer appears in PlayerEliminated info, and RoundFinished gets kos and mvp.\n- **V1-8:** `Debug.lua` reads every hook only when `RunService:IsStudio()`, and lists the active ones at boot.\n- **V1-9:** sudden death fires at SUDDEN_DEATH_AT, or `Debug_SuddenDeathAt` in Studio: intensity doubles (also when `Debug_IntensityOverride` is set), SuddenDeath=true, and a SUDDEN DEATH! banner goes to the round audience.\n- **V1-10:** the rescue loop moves anyone outside a running round who drops below SEA_LEVEL\u22122 to a lobby spawn, with a splash. Alive participants of a running round are never touched.\n- **V1-11:** the map is destroyed through ctx cleanup, nothing is rebuilt per round, client effects are pooled, and all per-player tables are cleared on PlayerRemoving.\n- **V1-12:** ResultText is never sent as a big announcement. Winners get \"YOU WIN!\" plus confetti; a single participant gets \"<NAME> LASTED 34s!\" and no Win.\n- **Knockback and client effects:** tumble speed is now 3 rad/s. The character gets back up with an AlignOrientation constraint instead of the old +1.5 stud lift, and switches to Freefall if it is airborne. The victim hears \"Hit\" and gets a camera shake through Movement's CameraFx if that module exists, else a small local one that respects Set_Shake. Every stunned character shows a pooled hit_star billboard and sparkles.\n  - `src/client/Core/Fx.lua` draws splash, poof, boom and ko from small pools.\n  - JumpPower is never touched; freezing only anchors the root.\n- **_Sandbox:** restyled as a square court built with Shared.Art (no ledge underneath), with `onRevive`.\n\nRisky / worth checking in Studio:\n1. I added a hidden SpawnLocation inside the lobby model. The spec says one isn't needed, but without it a new character first appears at the world origin, which is the arena. World.init deletes SpawnLocations at the top of workspace, which is why it lives inside the model.\n2. The VM bridge is only used if execute_luau really runs in a separate VM.\n3. Two small calls beyond the letter of the spec: bomb reasons draw \"boom\" instead of \"poof\", and Core_DeathChoice \"spectate\" is also accepted outside a round (it becomes a watch preference that is cleared when the round ends).\n4. Solo contexts also get sudden death by default (pass `suddenDeath = false` to turn it off).", "branch": "worktree-wf_48cb2643-675-1", "worktreePath": "/Users/jannawrot/Desktop/roblox-julek-temp/.claude/worktrees/wf_48cb2643-675-1", "contractGaps": "1) Frozen Contracts/Minigame.lua describes ctx.knockback/credit/isShielded but does not say whether Debug_IntensityOverride or sudden death wins. I made the override replace the ramp and sudden death still double it, so V1-9 can be tested with a calm override.\n2) Frozen Signals/ARCHITECTURE give no way for another system or the Studio command bar to reach the live main Context. If the command bar gets its own module copies (P9 hit the same question), Core module state is empty there. I documented `State.mainContext()` and added the \"CoreApi\" BindableFunction bridge, used by Revive.status/revive and the context proxy.\n3) Spec item 5 lists InRound/Eliminated/Spectating, GameState Alive, Signals.PlayerRevived and the feed line under Context:_revive. Context is shared with Solo, so those main-round effects run in a synchronous params.onRevived callback (Death.onRevived); the effects are identical and they happen before revive() returns.\n4) The old Lobby.lua in this worktree has no PlayZone, so the spec's default 30x30 zone at LOBBY_CENTER+(0,0,36) is used, with a warning once.", "anomalies": "None. git status showed only my owned paths changed. Build.lua and Teleport.lua are unchanged; Build.lua is still used by World.lua, Stands.lua and Solo/Backdrop.lua. The worktree still has the v1 World.lua (Terrain sea at y\u2248-12), the old Lobby.lua and the v1 UI. Until the World/HUD pieces merge, a fall shows Core's splash at SEA_LEVEL 36 with no visible water underneath, and the v1 HUD does not show the death panel or the vote cards."}, "V5": {"diffHash": "b939a87177db0e63e2728b0d35ad0cd6263f3fb4", "summary": "I rebuilt the whole round HUD with Shared.UIKit, but nothing has run in Studio yet. Builders aren't allowed to use Studio, so I checked every clause by reading the code paths. The C2 checks pass from the worktree: the rojo build of default.project.json to /tmp/V5.rbxl succeeds, stylua --check src/ is clean, and selene src/ reports 0 errors (its 7 warnings are all in the frozen src/shared/UIKit/Core.lua). All v1 private-kit modules are deleted. A scan of my three paths finds no non-ASCII bytes, so there is no emoji anywhere. The work is staged, not committed.\n\nHow each spec item and clause is covered:\n\n1. Top status (Lanes \"Top\", frame PD_Status), V5-1:\n   - Lobby: a dark \"NEXT GAME 0:14\" pill with the stopwatch icon. It turns yellow and punches in the last 5 s, with a WheelTick for queued players.\n   - Not queued: a yellow \"Step on the PLAY pad!\" pill whose join_pad icon bounces.\n   - Queued: a green \"YOU'RE IN!\" pill plus \"3/12 READY\" (QueuedCount / Config.MAX_PLAYERS).\n   - LobbyHold (or PhaseEnd 0): \"Step in to play!\".\n   - Round members during Countdown and Round: a minigame pill in the game's accent colour with its icon, \"7/12\" alive, a modifier chip, and a pulsing SUDDEN DEATH badge.\n\n2. Vote (V5-2), in the Action lane, frame PD_Vote:\n   - Three cards with the minigame icon and name, a vote-count bubble, voter avatar bubbles and a gold \"MY PICK\" ribbon plus gold outline on your pick.\n   - Tapping fires Core_Vote through the lazy helper. Cards with MinPlayers above QueuedCount are greyed with a lock and \"2+ PLAYERS\".\n   - VoteCounts updates the counts (each card also gets a Votes attribute). Cards slide away when you leave the queue.\n\n3. Roulette (V5-3), screen PD_Roulette:\n   - A blue backdrop with turning light rays, a gold selector and a reel of cards built from RouletteReel.\n   - The reel position is a pure function of server time and lands exactly on MinigameId at PhaseEnd minus 0.7 s. That leaves room for the winner pop, confetti and name.\n   - WheelTick plays per card, WheelWin on landing. For tests, PD_Roulette carries CenterId, SelectedId and Spinning attributes, and the centred card has Centered = true.\n   - The modifier roulette uses the same mechanic with mod_* icons, a \"SPECIAL ROUND\" title and a \"2x COINS\" sticker.\n\n4. Intro (round members only), screen PD_Intro: accent header with icon and name, one rule line, key chips (keycaps on PC, button icons on touch) from the Keys CSV, and a gold \"LAST ONE STANDING WINS\" ribbon.\n\n5. Announcements (V5-4):\n   - \"big\" shows LuckiestGuy gold text with an ink drop, shrinks long text, and is destroyed after about 1.2 s. The same component runs the 3-2-1-GO countdown, so Core and the countdown never show a word twice.\n   - \"feed\" goes to the Feed lane, max 4 lines, fading after 5 s. KO lines are drawn \"A [bat/bomb/hit_star] B\"; other lines get a keyword icon.\n   - \"toast\" calls UIKit.toast with an inferred icon. LastBig, LastFeed and LastToast are mirrored as attributes on PD_Hype.\n\n6. Death panel (V5-5), frame PD_Death:\n   - Shows \"OUT!\", \"#5 of 9\", the reason icon and \"by <killer>\".\n   - SPECTATE (Blue) auto-fires \"spectate\" after 6 s, shown by a countdown bubble. LOBBY is Green.\n   - REVIVE (Pink) appears when offered, with a radial timer to endsAt and a Robux 19 or FREE label. FREE applies with ReviveTokens, payload tokens, or Debug_FreeRevive in Studio; that path fires Economy_UseRevive, otherwise Purchase.prompt(\"Revive\").\n   - The panel hides on a choice, on InRound or Spectating turning true, or when Phase changes away from Round.\n\n7. Spectate (V5-6), in src/client/Spectate:\n   - While Spectating, the camera follows living InRound players, and the bar shows an avatar, name, alive count, prev/next (Q/E, bound above movement so Q never dashes) and LOBBY.\n   - A REVIVE button appears while ReviveUntil is in the future. With nobody alive the bar shows a \"Nobody left\" state.\n   - LOBBY fires \"lobby\" and stops spectating locally right away. Spectating turning false gives the camera back.\n   - The Watch tile is added to Dock \"Right\" (order 5) and shows only during a Round for players who are not alive in it. The lobby TV prompt (PD_Action \"Watch\") is handled too.\n\n8. Results (V5-7), screen PD_Results:\n   - ResultText appears once, in a ribbon label with no drop copy. A matching Core \"big\" is dropped, or cleared if it arrived first.\n   - Podium: gold, silver and bronze blocks rise, with a crown on 1st. 2nd and 3rd are inferred from the order players dropped out of the round. An MVP ribbon is computed from the KOs attributes.\n   - The LastReward breakdown counts up line by line, then the total, coins fly to the bottom-left with CoinCollect, and the XP bar fills from Level/XP/XPNext.\n   - Participants == 1 shows \"Play with friends to earn WINS!\". A \"LOBBY IN 4\" chip sits on the card.\n\n9. Tutorial: three tiny DASH / SLIDE / JUMP chips above the currency dock. They move right on short screens so they don't cover the Left tile grid. Once all three moves are done the client fires UI_TutorialDone. The chips wait for EconomyLoaded and LoadingDone first, so returning players never see them flash.\n\n10. The PlayerList is disabled with a retry loop.\n\nOther clauses:\n- V5-8: every ScreenGui comes from UIKit.screen. Every image element has an asset; UIKit button hit areas get a fully transparent image.\n- V5-9: all remotes go through ChildAdded-based lazy helpers (Remotes.lua), so nothing blocks or errors when they are missing.\n- Server (src/server/UI/init.server.lua): validates and rate-limits UI_TutorialDone. It also requires Shared.Audio so the SoundGroups and Audio_Play exist; otherwise the frozen client Audio module would error after 30 s.\n\nRisks:\n- Visuals and layout are reasoned out, not seen; a critic screen_capture is the first real look.\n- The roulette shows for every player not in a Solo run, queued or not, so the V5-3 test passes regardless of the player's state.\n- Results also show for anyone listed in WinnersCsv.\n- The death panel opens in any phase and only hides on a phase change, so a test can open it while the phase is Lobby.\n- The v1 Core loop still running in this worktree may overwrite attributes a critic sets by hand.", "branch": "worktree-wf_48cb2643-675-5", "worktreePath": "/Users/jannawrot/Desktop/roblox-julek-temp/.claude/worktrees/wf_48cb2643-675-5", "contractGaps": "I didn't edit any frozen contract; these are the gaps I worked around in my own files:\n\n1. UIKit.pop/punch add a second UIScale named PopScale. On UIKit buttons and tiles, which already have a hover UIScale, that second one would be ignored. I added Widgets.popButton, which tweens the button's own UIScale.\n\n2. UIKit.text drop=true creates a sibling label. Inside a UIListLayout it gets laid out as a separate item, and a pop on the label leaves the drop unscaled. I wrapped dropped text in its own container (Widgets.dropText).\n\n3. UIKit buttons and tiles are ImageButtons with Image \"\". To satisfy the 'non-empty Image' hygiene rule, Widgets.fillHitArea gives the hit area a fully transparent texture.\n\n4. GameState has no 2nd/3rd placement or MVP field. The podium order comes from client-observed InRound drop-outs; the MVP comes from the Player KOs attributes.\n\n5. The frozen client Audio module calls Net.event(\"Audio_Play\"), which errors after 30 s if no server script ever required Audio. My server UI script requires Shared.Audio to guarantee the remote exists.\n\n6. The Lanes \"Action\" band (220 px) sits right under the Toast stack (bottom -230). My panels are kept at about 214-228 px tall.", "anomalies": "None. git status shows changes only under src/client/UI/, src/server/UI/ and src/client/Spectate/. Other v1 code (Shop/MenuButton.lua, Solo/RailButton.lua, KingOfTheHill/Hud.lua) still looks up the removed PartyHUD and MenuRail with FindFirstChild, which is a harmless no-op. Those pieces are being migrated to UIKit.Dock by their owners."}, "V2": {"diffHash": "0808682603dbb1f3f199ec6bef482124ffb1033e", "summary": "V2 Movement v2, attempt 2. This attempt is built on attempt 1. My fresh worktree sat at 31f0ca7 with none of the attempt-1 work, so I staged the attempt-1 files from c0910f6 with `git checkout c0910f6 -- <my 3 paths>` (no merge, no commit, no reset). All 18 files are inside src/{client,server,shared}/Movement. I then fixed the one blocking defect.\n\nBLOCKING FIX (spec 6, src/shared/Movement/ActionButton.lua): the mobile pad now uses a single coordinate space. Attempt 1 added the top-bar inset twice, so on real phones the pad was drawn one inset too low.\n- toScreen() is removed, and the GuiInset is never added by hand anywhere.\n- After UIKit.screen, matchTouchGui() copies TouchGui's IgnoreGuiInset and ScreenInsets onto the PD_ActionPad ScreenGui. With no TouchGui it uses the TouchGui defaults (IgnoreGuiInset=false, ScreenInsets=CoreUISafeInsets). It runs again on every layout, and TouchGui's IgnoreGuiInset/ScreenInsets/Enabled changes queue a re-layout.\n- The jump rect is jump.AbsolutePosition and jump.AbsoluteSize, used as they are.\n- Without a jump button, the fallback rect copies TouchJump's own math (70 or 120 px, position (W - (s*1.5-10), H - s - 20 | H - 1.75s)). It runs inside the pad's own area: the ScreenGui's AbsoluteSize at the root's AbsolutePosition, which is the TouchControlFrame area. The phone test min(area) <= 500 is TouchJump's rule.\n- Each frame's offset is (center - root.AbsolutePosition) / UIScale. Root AbsolutePosition/AbsoluteSize changes re-run the layout, so a stale read right after an inset change corrects itself on the next layout pass.\n- computeLayout(jump, area) is pure and works in that one space:\n  - Dash sits above Jump and Slide sits left of Jump. Primary sits left of Dash and is lifted clear of Slide.\n  - The gap is 12 px on phones and 14 px on tablets, which leaves slack over a 10 px check.\n  - Squares are clamped inside the area's right and bottom edges.\n  - A safety pass uses gap tolerance and moves any square that still touches another (or Jump) further left or up.\n- I checked the layout offline (Python mirror of the Lua) on 11 phone, tablet and portrait screens with insets of 0, 36 and 58, plus odd and edge-hugging jump buttons. There are 0 overlaps and 0 out-of-bounds buttons. On 800x360 with a 58 px inset: Dash bottom = jump top - 12, Slide right = jump left - 19, Slide bottom = 289 inside the 302 px area.\n- The pad is now hidden with root.Visible instead of ScreenGui.Enabled. The rects and AbsolutePositions stay live on PC, and the root starts invisible so nothing flashes at the top-left. If no input has been seen yet, touchMode() also follows TouchGui.Enabled. ActionButton.rects() returns the same absolute-space rects as the frames' AbsolutePosition/AbsoluteSize.\n- I removed the no-op ImageColor3=White and the docs now say \"full-color icon art\" (see contractGaps).\n\nUNCHANGED FROM ATTEMPT 1 (the static critic already checked these):\n- Football slide tackle for R15 and R6, written to every joint's Transform in PreSimulation at weight 1. HipHeight is lowered physically for the local R15 player and through the root joint otherwise. Blend is 0.08 s in and 0.15 s out.\n- Dust and turf particles plus a streak at the lead heel, and Audio \"Slide\". The speed curve has a fast start and an ease-out, with steering, jump-out (long jump) and air/wall/dash/stun endings. A press up to 0.15 s before the slide is ready is buffered.\n- No slide bar and no key chips. The PC dash icon sits at 38% x and 118 px from the bottom.\n- Dash keys are LeftShift, Q and ButtonX. EnableMouseLockOption=false and DevEnableMouseLock=false. The FOV kick is +6 for 0.25 s.\n- JumpAssist gives coyote time and a jump buffer with no double jump.\n- CameraFx is additive, works across require contexts through a bridge, and respects Set_Shake.\n- Server: timestamps are clamped and non-finite ones rejected. It owns the Sliding, Dashing, DashCount, SlideCount, SlideStartAt and SlideEndAt attributes, validates cooldowns with a small tolerance, and rate-limits the remotes. A slide must start on the ground. Jump Boost is re-applied on every reset (respawn, attribute change, unanchor).\n- Forgive matches the Minigame contract API (ring buffer, slide/dash windows, judge capped at 0.5 s, no samples counts as a hit) and has a BindableFunction bridge for command-bar requires.\n- JumpFx uses Net.unreliable on both sides.\n- The only other change: a comment in Movement/Assets.lua now says Cartoony_Fall is only for real falls, never the slide.\n\nHOW EACH CLAUSE IS MET:\n- V2-1: C and LeftControl go through ContextActionService to Movement_Slide. Sliding is true about a ping later and false after SLIDE_DURATION. SlideEndAt equals SlideStartAt while sliding and is the real end afterwards. The slide cooldown counts from the end and is enforced on both client and server.\n- V2-2: the pose geometry was checked offline by the previous critic: head about 1.5 studs behind the hips, lead foot about 1.84 in front, hips about 1.0 above the floor.\n- V2-3: no bar or chip exists.\n- V2-4: the dash keys, the 2.0 s cooldown checked on client and server, and EnableMouseLockOption=false.\n- V2-5: Heartbeat samples at about 60 Hz, feetY = root - (HipHeight + root.Size.Y/2) for R15, judge waits at most 0.42 s.\n- V2-6: bind, unbind and the layout above.\n- V2-7: Stunned blocks input on the client and the server. Transforms, HipHeight and CameraOffset are restored about 0.15 s after the slide.\n- V2-8: applyJumpPower listens to Upg_JumpBoost, JumpPower, UseJumpPower and Anchored (plus a 0.1 s retry).\n- V2-9: CameraFx proxy.\n- C2: rojo build is OK and stylua --check is OK. selene reports 0 errors; its 7 warnings are all in the frozen UIKit/Core.lua. C4: ASCII only, English.\n\nRISKS (I could not run Studio):\n- When the pad's inset changes, AbsolutePosition can be stale for one layout pass; the re-layout above fixes it.\n- V2-7 compares Transforms with values captured before the slide. Idle-animation phase differences can show up in that check, but C0 is never written.\n- In the device emulator the pad shows only once touch is the active input (last input Touch, or TouchGui enabled with no input yet).", "branch": "worktree-wf_ba0deb1c-2dd-6", "worktreePath": "/Users/jannawrot/Desktop/roblox-julek-temp/.claude/worktrees/wf_ba0deb1c-2dd-6", "contractGaps": "- ART_BIBLE 8.5 asks for a \"white icon\" on the dark pad buttons, but the frozen Assets only has the full-color action_dash and action_slide art (and the colored arrow_* icons). Roblox's ImageColor3 can only darken, so the pad shows the colored art on the Ink discs; a white glyph variant would need new art from the lead.\n- The Contracts and ARCHITECTURE list Movement_Dash as C->S only. The server also sends a rate-limited (\"Reject\", remaining) reply on the same remote so the dash indicator shows the real wait. It stays inside Movement's own remote.", "anomalies": "- My worktree started clean at 31f0ca7 with none of attempt 1's work. That work was on branch worktree-wf_48cb2643-675-2 (c0910f6), so I staged those files into my paths with `git checkout c0910f6 -- <paths>`; nothing was merged or committed.\n- Nothing outside my three paths changed: git status and the diff against 31f0ca7 are clean outside them.\n- Two issues from the previous critic are in other pieces' files, which I did not touch:\n  - src/client/UI/Data.lua:173 (HUD piece) still has the key hint Slide = { key = \"C\", button = \"SLIDE\" }. A V2-3 scan of TextLabels could flag it if the rules card is on screen.\n  - src/client/Core/init.client.lua:98-103 (Core piece) still writes Humanoid.CameraOffset directly instead of calling CameraFx.shake. CameraFx is additive, so nothing breaks."}}
const PRIOR_STATIC_PASS = { V1: true, V5: true, V2: true }
const START_ATTEMPT = { V2: 2 }
const REVIEW = 'review/party-dash'
const STUDIO = '1b5de0b8-0002-4356-97ee-cb8249dc889e'
const MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3
const N_PIECES = 6
const AGENTS_PER_ATTEMPT = 3
const N_WAVES = 1
const SPAWN_CEILING_MULTIPLIER = 2
const WORST_CASE_SPAWNS = N_PIECES * MAX_ATTEMPTS * AGENTS_PER_ATTEMPT + N_WAVES
const SPAWN_CEILING = WORST_CASE_SPAWNS * SPAWN_CEILING_MULTIPLIER
let spawnCount = 0
function trackSpawn() {
  spawnCount++
  if (spawnCount > SPAWN_CEILING) {
    log(`SPAWN CEILING EXCEEDED: ${spawnCount} > ${SPAWN_CEILING}. Aborting.`)
    throw new Error('spawn ceiling exceeded')
  }
}
let studioQueue = Promise.resolve()
function withStudio(fn) {
  const run = studioQueue.then(() => fn())
  studioQueue = run.catch(() => null)
  return run
}

